.TH SCHVIEW 1
.SH NAME
schview \- show the pages of a schematic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B schview
.I sheet.vec
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Schview
shows the pages of a schematic in a window, one at a time, smoothed,
khaki (#BBBB99) on black.
A page runs from its page record (page W H N) to the next; with more
than one, the top left names the page shown, and a part newly
selected, from stdin or by a click, shows its page; PgDn and PgUp turn
the pages with a part selected too.
The window's title is the absolute path of the file.
The sheet comes as
.IR vec (5)
from
.IR schdraw (1);
its text is drawn from the glyph table lib/fonts/nimbussans.txt, and
everything is drawn by OpenGL, smoothed by multisampling and its lines
shaded by their distance, in linear light.
.PP
It opens fitted to the sheet, as Space fits it; the wheel zooms round
the pointer and the left button drags the view.
A click within 3 pixels of the box of an element of a part (its
symbol's body, or one of its texts: designator, value, pin numbers)
selects the part, of the smallest such element under the pointer, and
prints
.B select
.I NAME
on stdout; a click on none clears the selection here alone and prints
nothing.
The selected part, its symbol, pins and labels, is drawn light cyan
(#A0FFFF): its relative luminance, 0.86, is 1.8 times the khaki's, 0.48,
so the change shows without color too.
The keys:
.PP
.RS
.nf
c           center the selected part; again, with nothing
            changed in between, zoom in two times about it
C           zoom out two times about the middle of the window,
            centering nothing
Space       fit the sheet: its frame at the edge of the window
F5          read the file again, the view kept; Loading...
            in the upper right corner meanwhile
Esc         deselect, here alone; hide the help
?           a help of the keys, on and off
q           quit
.fi
.RE
.PP
It reads commands on stdin, a line each:
.B select
.I NAME
selects,
.B select
clears (for scripts: the viewers never send it), and
.B center
is c;
.B shot
.I file
draws the next frame into a PPM picture;
.BR "page next" ,
.B page prev
and
.B page
.I N
turn the pages.
The input of the window is taken before each command, so a picture
shows all the keys and clicks that came before it.
Cross-probing with
.IR pcbview (1)
is two FIFOs, each viewer's stdout the other's stdin.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
schdraw ch1.sch > ch1.vec && schview ch1.vec
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
pcbview(1), schdraw(1), vec(5)
